From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:24:28 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: a click on a command bar suggestion opens it, like
 Return
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In the ⌘T bar a click on a suggestion did nothing. The bar shows the
suggestions in Arc's order (what Return opens, then pages, then
searches), not the browser's. Return was mapped back to the browser's
line, a click wasn't: the row named its place in the shown list, the
browser found another match there, the URLs didn't agree and it
ignored the click. Nothing closed the bar or opened the new tab
either, and "Search YouTube" on a row went nowhere (keyword-click had
no listener here).

The searchbox now takes the clicks on its rows itself (before the
rows' own handlers): a click acts like Return on that row; a middle
click or ⌘-click (Ctrl elsewhere) opens it in a background tab and
leaves the bar open with what was typed (Arc); "Search YouTube" enters
that site's search in the bar, as "youtube ⇥" does (Chromium's keyword
chip when Meridian has no mode for it). Remove and action buttons on a
row name the browser's line too. A press on a row keeps the focus in
the field.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
